<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quintus Caecilius Metellus Macedonicus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 210–115 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Metellus Macedonicus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quintus Caecilius Metellus Macedonicus was a Roman general and statesman. As praetor in 148 BCE he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andriscus">Andriscus</a>, the pretender who had briefly revived the Macedonian monarchy, ending the Fourth Macedonian War. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-roman-province">Macedonia</a> was then organised as a Roman province, closing the period of the four Macedonian republics. He was consul in 143 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quintus-caecilius-metellus-macedonicus.jpg" alt="Quintus Caecilius Metellus Macedonicus" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: British Museum · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Q._Caecilius_Metellus_Macedonicus,_as,_155-149_BC,_RRC_211-1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
